wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-gados-name = Gados
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-gados-desc = A server-room operator in black. He watches the servers and quietly complains about Kaiser.
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-gados-marker = Spawner: Gados
ent-MobWH40KFootfallGados = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-gados-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-gados-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallGados = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-gados-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-gados-line-1 = The servers survived the night shift. So did I, but Kaiser is already testing our endurance again.
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-gados-line-2 = The moment I closed the last ticket, Kaiser brought another. Apparently he is the one with the uninterruptible power supply.
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-gados-line-3 = Kaiser promised five minutes of work. His clock apparently needs repairs too.
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-gados-line-4 = The Mechanicus preserve knowledge; I preserve the server holding it. It gets backup power. Kaiser gave me another shift.
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-gados-line-5 = I had just sat down to finish my tea when Kaiser found another fault. I would like to believe that was a coincidence.
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-gados-line-6 = Kaiser asked me to check one cable. While the magi honour the machine spirit, I find where it lost contact again. The cable turned out to be longer than the rest of my shift.

wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-shieldcoreattendant-name = shield-core attendant
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-shieldcoreattendant-desc = A Mechanicus attendant watches the shield core and waits patiently for everyone to stop touching the settings.
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-shieldcoreattendant-marker = Spawner: shield-core attendant
ent-MobWH40KFootfallShieldCoreAttendant = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-shieldcoreattendant-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-shieldcoreattendant-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallShieldCoreAttendant = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-shieldcoreattendant-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-shieldcoreattendant-chat = The shield is holding. That is a technical term meaning nobody has touched the settings yet.

wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-smesmonitor-name = SMES technician
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-smesmonitor-desc = A Mechanicus technician checks SMES charge against the instruments rather than management's wishes.
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-smesmonitor-marker = Spawner: SMES technician
ent-MobWH40KFootfallSmesMonitor = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-smesmonitor-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-smesmonitor-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallSmesMonitor = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-smesmonitor-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-smesmonitor-chat = Charge is rising. More slowly than the list of consumers, admittedly. Still, that is two good news items in one report.

wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-toolsorter-name = tool custodian
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-toolsorter-desc = A Mechanicus worker sorts tools with a precision rarely shared by the people borrowing them.
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-toolsorter-marker = Spawner: tool custodian
ent-MobWH40KFootfallToolSorter = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-toolsorter-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-toolsorter-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallToolSorter = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-toolsorter-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-toolsorter-chat = The spanners are sorted by size. If yours is called 'the one I borrowed yesterday', we will need further diagnostics.

wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmosconsoleoperator-name = atmos console operator
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmosconsoleoperator-desc = A Mechanicus operator monitors pressure and leaks at the atmos console.
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmosconsoleoperator-marker = Spawner: atmos console operator
ent-MobWH40KFootfallAtmosConsoleOperator = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmosconsoleoperator-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmosconsoleoperator-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallAtmosConsoleOperator = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmosconsoleoperator-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmosconsoleoperator-chat = Everything is sealed for now. I like reports where 'atmosphere' is not followed by 'outside'.

wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmoscylindertechnician-name = gas-cylinder technician
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmoscylindertechnician-desc = A Mechanicus technician checks cylinders and gas-line settings. Unexpected mixtures are unwelcome.
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmoscylindertechnician-marker = Spawner: gas-cylinder technician
ent-MobWH40KFootfallAtmosCylinderTechnician = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmoscylindertechnician-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmoscylindertechnician-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallAtmosCylinderTechnician = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmoscylindertechnician-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmoscylindertechnician-chat = The mixture is set. Please do not add 'a little more to be sure'. Gases have no sense of moderation.

wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmosstandbyrepairman-name = standby atmos repairman
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmosstandbyrepairman-desc = A human repairman waits in the passage, ready to attend a faulty gas line.
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmosstandbyrepairman-marker = Spawner: standby atmos repairman
ent-MobWH40KFootfallAtmosStandbyRepairman = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmosstandbyrepairman-name }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmosstandbyrepairman-desc }
ent-MarkerWH40KFootfallAtmosStandbyRepairman = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmosstandbyrepairman-marker }
    .desc = { wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-marker-desc }
wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-atmosstandbyrepairman-chat = I am not idling. I am the backup system. While everything is intact, I have the most convincing work report.

wh40k-footfall-mechanicus-marker-desc = Persistent source for a Footfall engineering NPC. The arrow previews facing; place seated actors on their intended chair's tile, with no exact centre alignment required.
